emoves a non-contributory tile, preserving the T5-6-7 chow and T3 pair for hand development.  \nReason: B2 is not part of any potential chow or pung, while retaining T3 (pair) and T5-6-7 (concealed chow) strengthens future meld possibilities. Discarding an honor tile like J2 is less ideal as it reduces flexibility for higher-point patterns.  \nAnswer: Play B2"}
